<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Article> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/headline> "My Life"@en .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/url> "https://tplegacy.net/my-life/" .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/sameAs> <https://n2t.net/ark:/68749/my-life> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/datePublished> "1978-03-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/dateModified> "2026-02-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/description> "\nBelvedere, New York\n\nAll of you have your own \"selves.\" Could you say whether that \"self\" is precious or trivial, good or bad? I'm sure each of you will answer that your \"self\" is precious and good. Many might even say that, though they do all kinds of evil, they still consider themselves good.\n\nMa"@en .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/publisher> <https://tplegacy.net/#organization> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/inLanguage> "en" .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/> .
<https://tplegacy.net/my-life/> <http://schema.org/timeRequired> "PT44M"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#duration> .
