<https://tplegacy.net/heaven-and-us/> <http://schema.org/description> "\nBelvedere\n\nIn Oriental philosophy, the word \"heaven\" connotes huge and noble things, while \"earth\" connotes small, lowly things.\n\nHowever, this distinction came to exist because of the fall of man; if there had been no fall, there would be no such difference between heaven and earth.\n\nWhen we speak"@en .
